Units of Measure

Resource Unit

Resource Unit is a unit of measure by which the Program can be licensed.
Sufficient entitlements must be obtained to cover every resource managed by,
processed by, or related to the use of the Program.

Asset

Asset is a unit of measure by which the Program can be licensed. An Asset is
any tangible resource or item of value to be managed, including production
equipment, facilities, transportation, IT hardware and software. Licensee must
obtain entitlements for the total number of Assets accessed, scanned or managed
by the Program.

Entitlement Restrictions:
  If Licensee is using the Program to manage IBM Security Guardium S-TAP on
  z/OS, entitlements are calculated at 1 Asset for every 5 Value Units (VU) of
  Million Server Units (MSU).

Conversion Entitlement Details:
  Guardium Data Protection      - 1 Asset / 300 RU
  Guardium Vulnerability Assessment - 1 Asset / 40 RU
  Guardium Quantum Safe         - 5 Assets / 1 RU
    (Note: As of IBM Guardium Data Security Center v4.0, new RU entitlements
     purchased on or after June 2, 2026 may no longer be converted to Asset
     entitlements for Guardium Quantum Safe.)

